Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
A gauche oppressor, they lace my eyes so tight,
A punishment weak to shame, unvaried,
Wasted, robbed, undone, stained with envy.
Alas, to blind me, your gentle words shall truthfully,
Yet take me elsewhere, in darkness,
As death consumes life, while yearning for your profound love.
  Yet, still, cherish life so deeply,
  My sorrow is one hellacious despair,
  When every thought hinders, ignites anew.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
Extraction from my body a sickness that can never be cured?
The medicine I'd use to maintain
Your purity after this war should require me;
