So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine will not forbid,
Truth will steal from me, my act is in no condition different than before.
O, welcome, let him lie.
He, in deed, lives and wavers between consent,
Like snow-kissed matrons,
Gods forbid me to lie in deepest debt,
And so I do declare, his truth is his brand.
Yet, lies of this kind might lie,
Ageing among graves where our voices die,
Blest and wild days begotten past.
  So let my lieblings deceive thee, thy truth I corrupt.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
