Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
And lo, your beauty is but luck,
Good beauty but random chance,
And if a stranger shows me your face, no disgrace,
No remorse I can find,
For if I break the law of your lovely plight,
All my vows and sanctities have been wilted,
And your precious one is unguarded,
Hidden from the common gaze,
Unspoken, given life, unconfessed,
Embraced, proud, esteemed, bright.
  A simple act of love, with grace and harm,
  Shall keep you, a beacon in the night, bright.


