Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
These rude mourners, mounted on the wind,
Of empty graves, full of mourners' disgrace.
In pity's guise, they stand, weeping,
And rightly so, they do, aware,
Of thy fair complexion, tamed by pity's cruel hand,
Such mourners' faces, in pity's guise,
