Lest sorrow lend me words, and words expresswise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express
My deepest longing, beyond the reach of common earth.
If thou wouldst but hasten from sorrow, grasp
The burden of sorrow with ease,
And draw it close to the instant, recognize
The fleeting moment, the solemn fact;
In this continual flow, discern
The fleeting moment's zenith, gently guiding
