In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
That spies their loves on thee, who doth spy.
To swear against thyself, I dare not deny,
My own love, such vile a crime,
That every blot of faith, both civil and religious,
Cannot compare with thy outward grace.
In truth, 'tis true that I love thee in sort,
That I adore thee in kind, with my own fall,
But that's not the love that spake.
O, what a false heaven hath made heaven,
A tormented home, where every blot fears,
In thy darkness, thy love strangely sketched.



