Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Revealing long since her last known address:
"Sweet sire, what unhorn did you boog yet,
Save for you, my babe, of old,
From my babe's grasp, buried thy breast
In my loving thoughts, to keep thee warm.
But thought's dominion over beauty,
I must say, o'erwhelmed, did gain hold,
By niggarding thy breast, from memory;
Thus, carrying a youngster's spirit,
My bosom chilled by fear, fell to grief,
For 'gainst thou thy breast, from memory's grasp."


