Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May access to thee.
The charter of my heart is so narrow
That I have lost all control, and yet by your grant
I am bound to keep, an ever-renewing lease.
That I have abandoned thee, this slander doth
Lay bare in knowledge of thy defect,
