Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Diverting light on the plight of the poor.
My lips, which bear the lament,
At thy cruel hand, have writ a poem,
A mournful hymn to me, thy fate!
I'll not let envy taint my thought,
While thoughts of thee dwell in sleep,
Soothsayers' sorrow will surely make it seem
Thy name, when I'm astray, ensnared by its care.
  If thy beauty shines like mine,
  Then I'll not mourn, while other schemes are spent.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And in your power to compel me to share
The story of love and tear down walls apart?
Have you not seen those cruel scribes
Who sift through the scriptures to paint their tales?
Whoso restrains me, let my name rest where my body shall meet,
No longer causing me much grief,
For you, now my earth, and all my living blood
Cannot compare with the beauty of your tire.
  Yet, if you would but embrace, step inside,
  And let your heart take its part in love's story.


