If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Thy foe, my dearest ill, now deemed fair,
Disdains the beauty that he should break free,
And, like the canker from the dower,
Feeds on the rose that grows rich and fades with it.
Make thy desire met with true love,
A love-school, in which all vice is dressed,
That every tongue, the alluring of it,
Within thine own soul, by me taught doth thrive,
  And thou, that enamored whore, woos me here.


