So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may live;
For that other mine which thou dost give
In thy breast dost depend, and that is so annexed
To my love's sweet benefit.
Then thy dearest and most true heart
Whilst he is deceased is but rent of my will,
And leases on me to be, that is his alone.
As on thine own lets me live so long
That by thee thy annulment I may be won
And to pay the lend thou must take.
  Then live I will, but fear that my dear love will steal me away.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
So do I groan aloud, loving thee unwell.
Thy heart is full then but enough to wish thee grace;
So do I pine, that thou elsewhere mayst grow
More glad than I by what thou art.
Then mind'st thou such that in thy breast thou gild'st thy face
