If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Thou canst not vouchsafe my coming near,
Although in the depth of thine eye I lie,
Knowing it must waken thy spirit, assured,
To suspect foulness in thy part, assured?
Till I am assured thou know'st it, and so,
To shun appearance like a deceived husband;
In hence, being sworn to lie, I seem innocent,
But in the decree of thy frown, I seem guilty,
