Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
But, Love, they misconstrue it, and make it seem
Like a tried-and-true thing.
To speak of things that are plain is not so,
To say of things that are truly so is false,
Lest I should look into false men's eyes,
And say they cannot tell the difference between thee and me.
But why should I question their eyes, though they see
To change the very things that we change in thee?
  Love, tell them thyself what thou desireth;
  I'll show thee how to make things seem new.


