Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may depend;
Thou dost give my life to another quest,
And that for thyself to breed another
In thee art much needed than my own desert.
Thou art the world's thievish wanton pawn
And only I in thee to breed that is
Another self to thy world, more chaste and more rare.
Thou hast drawn thy world and thy son to thine,
