Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Gentle on their sorrow, at thy sight's cruel glare.
Yet my soul cherishes thy sorrow, held in view,
Defying the gaze, of pity's effect,
As mourning becomes you, in every feature,
Then I find my heart's true place, shown to the blind,
Gazing on darkness, as the blind do attest.
