In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
That thou indirectly dost love those menaces which thou dost scold.
In others' wills, my nature's majesties are sung,
Though in mine own hearts each by others is swerving,
Not to thy unworthiness they aspire.
Yet in that my love most is dressed
Within the sacred dictations of my heart,
That nothing noble in me can claim a place,
Unless this general evil in me be done:
  All strong men in authority conspire,
  To this end I almost do defeat them.


