Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Sets thee free in the midst of thrall,
A chainsaw, to be loosed from freedom's grasp,
Takes her young one back, and begins
To wreak revenge on Fortune's dulling sway.
Beware, ladies, of this wickedness!
She can only detain, not eternally ensure.
  Thus, thou shalt be foiled, and she will be killed,
  For she who abhors thee will be foiled,
  In the very act of love, that breasteth still.


