If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Till I have strayed hence, leaving thee,
Thyself in the world, defiled, replete,
And left as a beacon in the night,
To wither and decay, as is thy soul,
In the course of this, not knowing the near,
Or at thy side, the hollow shall tell
