Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thy lips, which taught the world that night,
To love anew, as thine own, by shadows ensnared.
Yet, as mine eyes gaze on me, they find
No reason to love thee, as mine,
For I am as thy heart is, and they, knowing it,
Admit their mistake, and rightly so.
For I have loved thee, and they, in ignorance,
