When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And hang her praises in proud words of meekness.
But that she thinks me wise I do swear
That she knows well my days are days of youth and hate,
And that I never saw those cheeks dyed red
With malice in seeing men's habit.
I swear by this, and so many other things,
That I love her for she thinks me kind,
Though she thinks me of nothing holy.
  But then believe me, sweet love,
  Even that her heart may lie that I swear.


O, call not me to justify the wrong
