Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may depend;
For such are thy tenants now, as is thy son,
And for them my will is forfeit to thee.
Then can I have thy favor still more enjoy
By paying thy rent or on thy return,
For nothing else in this world can I gain;
But what I do possess, what I have not lose,
By willful choice of what I have found.
  Thus do I now surmount this storm,
  That all my wealth is in thee, and none can see it wrong.


