In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
That doth my soul in love dislike show.
For such false love in me is born of true hate,
Which in myself doth base hate assemble,
As well as in my nature's gross miscues tell.
So then thou false murd'rous eyes bestow'ring hate
On my life, my dearest and mine only wish doth lie,
A house of roses, in happy health sit.
  In me, that well may be known as thee,
  For whom thou dost hate in me is born this day.


