Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And still more than enough thy neglect will make seem
To grow another self in me, more genuine still.
Thou dost beguile the world, and she that cherishes thee
Will sourly approve thy defect, if sourly thou know
That she hath the will to make thee grow.
Thou hast my mistress' fortune, and she hath all the might
To make me another self, more genuine still.
Such is my love, to thee I so belong,
That every tongue that calls upon thy name
  Shall read ' me, or 'tis my will, to die.



If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
