So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may live;
For thy image is too fair for my worthless lays,
And I impair not how to make use of it.
Now then thou wilt be the fairest of all,
And I in hope will be the fairest man
Whilst he which in thy image lives,
For what's so fair that thou dost make so great?
Begger our appetites and our requests be
To thy sweet favor and to be king o'er.
  I will not complain that I am poor,
  Since that my deeds show that I am rich.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And for my vexation plagues me onwards;
So do I my worst, and do this with greater zeal
