Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And, O, blame thy sins when they see!
But why should my eyes be stained with mud?
They see but what is best,
And that is thy best self, to thee they swart.
Thou hast thy glass, 'tis my soul that doth view,
And my cheek to my inward pure shows,
Which is thine to my inward frown.
But why thy glass doth not clear thy picture,
Detrimmed by tears, and tears doth it disgrace?
  Thy tears doth steal the treasure of thy love.


