In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Which for myself doth love most, indirectly so.
That mine eye is not in thy heart to frown upon,
Nor mine own self-love to show thee how;
Neither for thyself to stop mine eye from smitten face
Thyself thyself to pardon thy wrong.
O, that our night of eyes might revenge,
To make love of thee more and more dull
Than in thyself to stop sleep from being paid.
  How like Eve's apple doth thy beauty grow,
  If thy sweet self would stop thy sweet self from growing.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
No need for symbols do I bear,
For in mine is my truth translated, out of sight.
Then may I proudly claim thy love,
Although in thy heart's design none is truly bright,
In mine is my soul's domain writ.
Who hath shown thee how to make my heart love,
Rising from the depths of despair,
To love thee more, as thou dost thine own part?
  The coward who woos the mad do enshrine
  In their wills, no love displayed is 't burliest.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
The bloody spur cannot provoke a tear,
Nor draw a sharp thought from a dream's pass.
No matter if my foot were on the farthest shore,
Or sunk within the ocean's deepest trench,
My thoughts would soar to explore,
The space where it desires to reach.
Alas, it dreams, and indeed, it is true,
That millions of strange dreams may spawn,
Dreaming of you, your beauty, and your might.
  But never say that you were kind to me,
  For I, in my thoughts, was butying with thee.


