Thou dost love another, whose part is most holy,
But that thou art not so swerving mayst thy soul suspect,
For whose part is often thy nobler part?
For where is thy nobler part, that thou dost love
So great, that thou art as fair to see as any man?
Or on thyself who for thyself so fair doth live,
To show what thou dost base love pay;
  And, proud as an antique book, shouldst appear
  To be an every-born thing, old.


