In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
That my eyes in thee spy these faults and look
In curious ways to discover what is best.
For if it be ill to me, why should I hate thee,
When my own true love hath shown thee how?
Or on thy defect, 'tis my love that I try
To wreak revenge, 'gainst myself a thousand groans,
And against myself, mostly I forget;
  But when the revolt takes leave of me,
  My love runs straight towards thee and I lose my sight.


