My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express
The beauty that words convey.
Pause for a moment, observe how things work,
And then return the favor:
Spare me the bitter hours of this endless dance,
Spare me the torment of days I've missed;
Waste not time upon the sweets of days long spent.
Silence stays at my side, as I mend
The wounds left by adversaries' cruel scythe,
Strengthen my healing skill with words that both aid.
  Yet, lest your affection flares, heed my advice,
  Amass clear remedy for all wounds I have yet dealt.


In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
