Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Spending all eternity in the chaos.
This woman of yours holds the flame she does bind,
Persisting through the nights, her eyes fixed,
Her heart is your purpose;
No other voice or judgment crumbles,
Save your love, which starts at a distant place.
I forever try to enshrine her love, purest soul,
Though we've lost ourselves in mire,
Her voice still rings, though it's changed from pitch;
  Her love remains steadfast, though we've changed it all.


