In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Whilst mine eye keeps secret the treacherous's dance.
To swear against me is to swear against myself,
And in this swerve sin lies practiced,
Thy lover's face, while mine eye keeps it still,
Despair's of false lips, false dalliance smeared.
I beseech my eye, 'tis true love, 'tis my grief to view,
That Love steals beauty away from my sight.
  For eyes can never perceive thee,
  Which hates me if I chance to blink.


