If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Yet look on thy transgression thou shalt not pardon,
For 'twas perjured are those that seek to prove
Thy virtue by thy deeds disgraced.
Be thou the vessel wherein thine false souls find release
Whilst on our trespass 'tis graved and sown,
Like a field where the false copies find their place,
Die to themselves, as thy trespass proves.
Thou hast lost the kingdom of thought,
Which on thy transgression leads to greater woes,
And 'twas reduced, as the crow flies,
Borne away on the winds that do torment thee.


