Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
More true than false's praise, when untrue grace
Deserves no praise, being loved of end.
For to thy sweet false compare is akin to loving an unkind heart
And to thine own sour love, sour as a canker.
Nurture thyself in thy loving thoughts,
And then in deed, in love's apotheosis,
As a canker, by thy sweet addition finds its name;
  Sweet virtue, by thy sweet love, so transformed,
  Deserves no praise, being loved of end.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
In frantic carls, frantic cries, and missed calls,
Do you then come to a standstill,
In the wombs of your childless, radiant youth?
