So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May choicest of times may lie.
But herein lies his good fortune, if I can find it not there.
So far for love my tears are now and gone,
The poison of my despair is now teeming,
And from the contagion of my plight I take shelter.
But then can no more my despair provoke;
Until I have built a new one,
With stories of love, and fear of new lies.
  Then may I proudly claim the love I bear,
  Until then, not to be cast away.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
