In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And my sense, the finer part of my power,
Makes mistakes with thoughts that tolls my soul.
The odor of passion kindles a thousand different jells,
In my sense, the most heinous sin found;
In actions tainted, mine is the most heinous crime,
And in my sin, my acquittal lies.
But if a god doth this unwavering justice,
In love's image, my acquittal lies,
And kindled this new woe,
  That binds me close, and slows my flow.


