Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thine eyes outshine the morning sun,
Bestowing graces on undeserved delight.
Yet my soul cherishes what they disdain,
For thy black is soothing, light and serene,
And when thy thoughts of love remove,
My soul finds soft joy amidst this sorrow.
Pity me, then, and I shall tell thee:
Thy eyes outshine the evening,
Attacking thy heart, with cruel spite.
  Lo, thus, I'll attest, and so,
  Kill 'em with gentle sorrow, I'll attest.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And force my dearest friend to weep for me?
Even if my heart were able, to force my friend to weep
For me, it still would not bring me to see you through.
It wrenches me from my own core, so I lose him,
Abandoning me to the world's cruel gaze.
Imprison my heart within your fortress chest
