Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thy complexion's shadow, like a cruel mistress, woe betwixt
My heart and gaze, enemies to love.
For all the beauties that I see,
Conserving thy heart, I scorn,
Yet none can claim to hold, a heart so bleak.
My heart is too gaunt, the view alone,
Conserving thy heart, I plead,
A tale of love, with sorrows and joy.
  Yet, in all this I plead,
