Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And force my dearest friend to share this grief?
To let my heart be marred by hate and scorn,
And to seek relief only the blind do witness
To sin and evil's face.
How can I then be truly grieved at,
And at thy touch, share this grief?
Even though I be blind, I know that
Thy heart's love is real,
And that its visage bears witness to change.
  If I but gaze, see darkness stilled,
  The world will weep for thee, my friend.


