Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
Another friend, now alive, takes her place,
And mother nature keeps her wealth displayed,
With eager fingers and yesterdays gone by.
So you, in solitude, take your leave,
Your child, your spirit's fresh delight,
And do what you desire, in your power,
To the earthbound primate who'll be your father's guest.
  Still, if you are lost, find your way,
  And come back home, my dear, you shall find
  A new, fresh life, and a warm embrace.


