Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thine eyes outshine the sun, in pity crowd.
Yet my soul, made sad, seeks solace in thy shade,
Seeking hope, in thy darkened throne room.
For to thy beauties my sorrow I send,
A token of my love's deep sorrow,
And to those lips that hold my heart, I send
Tokens of my love's deep despair,
With proud gestures, their despair fading.
  In sorrow's guise my heart and eyes share,
  And in thy darkness, my despair never fades.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to share this grief?
For you I have bound up a new plight,
A kinder, warmer, more inviting soul,
For in my friend's gaze, none can escape.
The dawn's first light, in heaven's broad expanse,
Nor the bright star that heralds twilight's hour,
Can match the solemn beauty of your glance
When you blot the heaven below.
  Or should I say, "Now I alone stand condemned,"
  To blot the earth with your eternal stain.


