Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
Than as enough doth my miser that churls his spoil;
And for that treasure thou dost give away,
The willing borrower of that would be most glad,
For that churl being tyrants find a way
To make his living by thine own sweet spoils filed.
That's for thyself to live in posterity
Than be contented that thyself doth live,
For that sweet lovingly graces thy living soul.
  Thou gav'st me thee to give away,
  Being all alone that thyself dost pay.


