Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
For the loveliest of votaries to grace,
With gentle, rhythmic grace granting time grace,
Time's finest jewel from Nature's binocular table.
Ponder the clock that tracks the fleeting hours,
For if no one else remains, let him in,
And let him in again, when Nature calls,
By Time's own unyielding hand she'll make history.
