Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Fast forward ten times your power, and do not harm again.
Bring gladness and sorrow as you take stride
And do what you wish, swift-moving shadow,
To the wide universe and all her passing pride.
But I forbid one wicked deed from you:
O, do not, when my beloved's eyes are full,
Creep in upon the heels of conquered pain;
Bestow not following darkness after storm,
To draw out fate's intended ruin's reign.
  But do thy worst, old friend; in spite of your harm,
