That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
To keep alive my heavy lids in the tomb
Of worth, though we both fell.
Yet, she loves me, knowing well my days
To indulge in her pretense, her untrue words
To my fall, which I did not consent.
I think she knows what with her eyes is allayed
