So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
Will depend upon thy granting.
The lease of my love is not to be rekindled
Within the realm of thought, but in mine own heart it
Is thinly stretched, and wide,
Wasting time and ruining riches on false compare.
He that levelest to me allows
My will to dry up his wealth, which I will lose;
He that is unaware what thy will
Is thinly stretched, and wide, doth give
My will to that purpose and thee.
  Receiving this will, I lose but his,
  And he that pays the rent cannot be blamed.


