Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
I, in love's terror, let your love's servant wither,
Just as a lover's hand takes from his knell.
I keep you close, but not forever tight;
For in your stead, time's deception takes hold,
And I lose you both to my will.
Then can you claim my love without my hand?
No, Lo, but in the very act of love,
