And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May rely upon thy deeds for my lays.
In him I confine all good looks and all pretense,
And for this trust I gave myself,
He is well aware, and lives upon this store.
When your treasure I have filled with store,
