So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May rely upon thy love's instigation.
For thee I give full heed to thy will,
And to the lark even so pays the toll;
Therefore he pays the debt in me
And pays it on purpose; the loan
Is not me but a surrenderer on the ground.
The title to thy love I can find
And on the lark even that pays it is aware.
  The judgment of thy worthiness I can see,
  And the judgment of thy sweet love I can see.


