Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
The thief of thy joy, in thy stead,
Lives alone, and waits for you, his peacekeeper.
Then may I boldly speak of love's fine grace,
Though thou control my heart's contentment;
Until then, thou shalt be hushed, my silence is broken,
By my unspoken vows, thou shalt be stol'n,
A lawful womanizer, far more deserving.
  Nay, do not, when I have left this place,
  Consider leaving thy love, even to the very edge.


