Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thy complexion, thy beauty's melancholy, in gloom;
My soul, theirs, has followed the sorrow of yore,
And found relief in thy remorse.
Yet eyes, being mourners, cannot grasp the weight of remorse,
Nor think the depth of love's deep plea,
