So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May depend upon thy love's will.
In many a story of worth, the false
Gift of thy will, the worthless conquest.
Then in the charter of my beauty I confine
My value to settle down again,
With those who have bought this store, so
Thyself thy sweet favor will depend;
So, to be sold I forfeit myself,
And that myself will be my debtor.
  A friend to thee is all my comfort,
  Since that use is all my own.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
Than that whose treasure thou dost desire,
And hath not paid thy due, yet am I dumb.
Thou art the tenth rupee fixed in my love's land,
And I, in love, hold it at a higher value,
Than thought that by thy will will would be a gain.
But why thy will not thou take this insignificant land?
Because thou art too kind, and for thy love there reigns,
Or to whom thy sweet love dost want, be it for thee.
  The cause of love is wanting, and so should that hate.


If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
