Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
So far for love my love's appeal, kind, fulfill;
Desire will fulfill the need, kindling need,
And love's sweet thought, though potent, will fulfill,
Unless this craving intensify desire.
Passion will fulfill the desire, kindling need,
Unless this craving intensify desire:
  Your eyes, though bright, may wander,
