Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
I hook thee up with that lovely April,
And use thee to fuel my beast,
Whilst I, poor but true, travel
And find that thou in me remain
Forgetting thy lover, who for thyself stays behind.
Then canst thou no longer be lame
Unless thou return my dear one's life bewailed,
And use my wit to fuel my hungry ghost;
  Yet do not so. I will wait for thee, and see
  The blessed enchantment that thy love will bestow.


