Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Adorned in black, their love forsworn,
With weeping and woe, they weep,
Their hearts entwined in despair and woe,
At the mercy of thine eyes,
Adorning themselves with such finesse.
Oh, let thy heart recount what I have surmounted,
My failings be my triumph,
The triumph of thy love, my vows fulfilling;
Though I may strip away, yet still face this pain,
  For in this plight, I am losing thee.


