Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To find the source of your spirit, expand
The one you touch, in all your jollity.
My silence, then, shall be but a gait,
Silent heralds of my heart's true quest,
Speaking for you, no quiet moment grieve.
I'll not let envy taint my heart,
To mark the rain on your cheek,
Nor find the taste of solitude a crime,
When you, my liege, have taken your leave.
  So true a follower is love, it bends
  To every whim, each twist and turn it lends.


