Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
Perched now atop life's joyous peaks you stand,
And many a fertile field, unplowed by hand,
Would gladly bear your image, true and grand.
So too, the sea, which with its eager increase,
Drained of the rain, and thus, more blessedly so,
Would bear your shape, its glory to trace.
A thousand streams, once but one of few,
Then fade to gray, as the seasons meet.
  In your absence, winter's grip stays fast,
  And in your shadow, I find sweet release.


