In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight it draws.
Therefore do I pine and surfeit day by day,
Each under-whelmed, my poor, willful heart
Whilst the fruits of love are loved or die as if by their own doing.
But your affection springs from your own core,
A thousand and ever growing,
In your affection, a thousandfold blessed are you.
  For thou dost lie with me,
  For I cannot love one for whom thou dost lie.


