Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the belovedliest of votaries in the bosom.
No need for haste, as a widow's tear
Does bind her husband to share this grief,
And weep afresh love, when it kills.
Then can no harm dare to stain the very wound,
To amend love's pure light, though it may stain the very ground.
O, what a gift, to share this love profound,
To cherish more the more I see amiss?
  But what's so steadfast that it fears no shift?
  Love's compass may point true, or veer adrift.


