Thou art as fair as in my seeing,
Finding thy worth a limit past my praise,
And therefore art enforced to seek anew
Some fresher stamp of the time-bettering days.
And do so, love; but when thy face
Times eclipses all men's loving parts,
Reveal five hundred cycles of the sun's whirl,
Might I discern the rud'st or gentlest grace?
  If thy unworthiness hath wrought this,
  More worthy am I to be loved above.


