Remaining steadfast, the semblance of a man is caught,
Thy haughty heart's thrall, a wretched servant to be.
  Only my affliction, thus far


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And my love's bond is weak, kind, and true.
For to this I often preside,
Thy looks disclose naught but sweetness, day and night.
And when they wink, 'tis with sobs,
That love may thrive and hearts in harmony stroke.
But that is not my love, though born of thee,
For in thy shadow, I find the truth:
Thy looks reveal naught but sweetness, day and night.
  Or if they sleep, thy looks disclose naught but sweetness,
  And yet, love's sweet memory grants.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the wide world, her jewels to be her wish.
So thou, in pursuit of dreams, abandon me,
Your child, to languish, unbent
With worry, wisdom, and fear;
A life unburdened, but not defeated,
To find peace with the world, her heart's abyss.
In so bold a path do I traverse,
My path Iaves her past, my weary soul behind,
But keeps my eye true, though my heart may wander.
  For if it brings my shadow,
  I'd never be alone.


