If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
So be my love, your true form is ever drawn
From thee, though in the flesh thou mayst move.
Thy looking glass, thy fading beauty doth deceive,
The creases on thy visage, purest of heart.
How far a modern blot would be my grave,
If thou couldst move with thy living gaze,
Leaving naught but barren plains where life had run?
  This thought is as a death, which cannot choose
  But weep to have that which it fears to lose.


