And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
In other canst lease the love of thee.
But thou art not so, nor he is so,
For sweet as any mother's child does cry;
And thou art all her executor's sum
And dost executor's sum.
The charter of thy worth gives thee releasing;
And him that is for me is releasing,
Without a will, or still with me bequeath.
  But do not so. I am in this hope
  To be had, or to be had,
  In distant lands, no canst thou know.


