Lest sorrow lend me words, and words expresswise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express
ThyOUGH, and patience, be the eloquence.
Roses have thorns, and silver fountains mud;
Clouds and eclipses stain both moon and sun,
And loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud.
All tongues, the voice of inner sighs,
Bestow the honor that you impart;
Yet, in thy sweet appearance, I do praise thee,
And thou, an obedient servant, stand
Upon thy sweet and gentle spirit.
  If some suspect of thy woe
