Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And I, in this, shall claim is right.
For this, for my sin against myself is born,
My virtue against myself against myself against myself.
For thee, my love, so never quietus,
Gives audience, as the true soul finds.
Grant me the right to love each day and every motherfied,
Whilst that I, in this service, shall boast,
Making my name my image whole.
  For thee, my name will be my love,
  And my heart, in harmony.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the chase and come back again,
In gladness and regret, I all too bestow
My strength and all my comfort,
For I, a flawed beguiler, no need to be your dearest
When I no longer able to raise my heart's ache.
O, that our love could have brought life,
A child begotten from love's kindle,
Who, in turn, would fly again,
For love's wing would give birth to my soul.
  But since my soul's journey is done,
  I'll not be alone.


