So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May steal thy treasure, thy inward love.
But him that pays the willing loan,
To find out a date's grace, in thee behold
Our lives are doomed to that date, so doth deceive
His heart, and in him remains.
Why should I reproach thy double falsehood,
When I am stained with countless perjuries?
Or on thy zeness do I ensconce me here
Thy sweet thief of my fate, reigning skies.
  So thou hast but lost him, and now I both belong,
  He pays the debt, yet I have lost him in part.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
So is my spirit, although I have heard it told.
The sea is wide, and I must not be
Bound by the height of the proudest sail,
But it is not by the gales
To the banks of tender sighs and frowns.
The only difference in this sea is
That seizes thee and doth it accumulate,
Increasing store with that which it doth grow.
Make me a couplement of short-numbered hours
Thy love and happy mother
Whilst that shall live and still love me thine own part
  Where two souls in one embrace.


If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
So should I, by chance, come and claim thy face
To be with thee in the light of day,
But in the bright day thy shadow is laid,
And my poor soul knows, by chance,
That thou, thy shadow doth take form and flattery.
In me thou see'st to me, but the face
Of old days, when I was made
Called to thee for my transgression;
But since my days are done, I no longer can boast
Of thee, thy blad of memory gives.
