Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Adorning ugliness and grief as fast as thou grow'st.
Yet those whose hearts are so as mine,
Whose hearts are so blessed, and they rightly do show,
Some of their faces, some of their heart,
To thee I send them from thy sight,
As I shall thee lead them from thy sight,
To share a single space,
The Earth may reclaim her place,
But my spirit, the nobler part, belongs to thee.
  Let those who are so blessed, and they are so,
  To share this grief's crown.


