Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To work the bloody world, unbless some mother's son,
Her bosom lives, and warms the clock,
Neglecting those that she should love the best,
Her skill now being found of favour,
And strength now hobbled, power rendered lame,
Art shackled, silenced by the powers that be,
Folly donning wisdom's cloak with ease,
Truth labeled simple, twisted and misused,
Goodness held captive, serving villainy.
  From these, she walks me, never bound,
  To keep up a lover's memory.


