Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As those who possess thee, through my gaze.
Yet in my sight, none so bright as mine,
No figure true, no wisdom quite so grand;
I, in my self-infatuation, do tie
My worth to eclipse all others in my sight.
Yet, my own eyes, in their own orbs,
Contend for right to claim thee, through the ages' cruel scythe.
  For thee, I paint my age with colors new,
  In self-delusion, seeking beauty true.


