Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And what is it composed, that is so blessed?
So, either by thy beauty they find their lie,
Thyself away are they so blind, and therefore they measure
By thy beauty, thy truth, thy faithfulness so rare.
Yet, Love, beware the allure of false, ephemeral fame,
