Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As those whose hearts are crushed by despair.
Yet in my gaze, heaven's will decreed
That thou shouldst forsake me, and should I forsake
My nobler self to my body's treachery.
My soul will raise quite a toll,
And in my sight, it will come to slay
The nobler spirit of my heart's true quest.
  And yet, in my sight, black is being made,
  And thence, through my sorrow, thou shalt be told.


