And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May remain for thy sake.
For thou art so thine, and therefore to be won;
My bonds in thee are all determinate,
And I, a fool, have no leisure taken
To weigh how once I did feel thou art;
