More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And for that which I in thee doth depend.
The sea, though it be wracked, I know it well;
And in that sea I confine
That it may hold me, though its height be measured,
And in that sea I confide,
