And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine.
Thy value in thy will, so great,
For how can I find a home in thee,
When thou dost give me a fitting garment,
And arts with thy sweet graces graced,
And puts apparel on my poor head,
And puts a spirit of youth in every shape,
Where wasteful Time debateth with Decay
To change my day of youth to sullied night;
  And, all in war with Time for love of you,
  As he takes from thee, I engraft
  A new self, ten times more loving and more temperate.


