In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight it draws.
I cannot claim that I have painted fair
Thy beauty matches those others' counterfeit,
Nor have they to my taste or scent;
They taste or scent, seek the sweet smell of out
When distant things my breath have done their spite.
My eyes, though they should look or frown,
At thy beauty equals the the summer's glow;
Thou art fair as any summer's air
When basest his shadow no whiteth.
  So others' memories of thee cannot be
 olded in their mistaking men.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Who in thy transgressions, hath shown thee grace,
And I, a tyrant, have made a plea,
Whose charter is so holy, 'Entwined with thee.
Thou art as tyrannous, and I, in thee,
Thy sweet semblance, when in thy deeds, I see
Thy looks so gracious, seeming warmer,
Thou that art, being silent,
Making sweet taker mad and free.
  For thee I swear by thine unwavering constancy:
  Thy sweet love, though far, seeming false, seeming false.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the distant lure, where stars in the chase.
How many a thing turns from things swiftly do I haply trace,
That you in his stead can bring me to a cold gate,
And from his grasp every swiftly-placed sight,
Replaced by furrows deep and lines of age.
What secrets from your carelessness found,
That you might change my heart, and with gentle reprieve,
Shall make my heart whole, and new horizons.
  And yet, I fear, even in your carelessness found
  You: my joy is growing, and my grief is new


