In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
For thee my eyes in heaven adore report.
But to thy virtuous deeds I add one falsehood,
As I, a fool, in love's deadly game,
Thou false heart's sweet confidant doth confirm.
For if it smears my love, true love says thine,
Faith disdains the smearing, for love's sweet act
Divides love, and makes naught but foes and perjured.
  And thus, in deceit, my love is as strong as a lion,
  And on thy darkness, I lean.


