One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Lending no spirit but that of her hidden woe;
So you, like a mother hen abandoned, run
To the abandoned house, to find out
What grief her young ones have become,
And what joy they left in vain;
For all the joy and sadness I have seen
Is but the tinge of abandonment left in me,
Like a mother's regret, a knife's plight,
She sharpens her focus, and lets her child go.
  But you, abandoned, and longing, cannot be soeled
  Away; your worth is your own, and only.


