Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the place where it had its welcome, unconfined.
So you, like a wary mother, stay close
To your child, who, though you abandon,
Does follow you, unseen, to his destiny.
No fear can touch me, for I grasp
The fortitude that you, in your care, unloosed,
And under your guidance, he grows strong.
  But still, there I stand, unwavering, with fear,
  For my child, who, in your care, grows bold.


