Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And in that they err, just as I.
They look upon truth with eyes that look on might,
And, so they blindly, blindly pursue
The star that leads them far from truth and clear.
But why do you follow this path,
That leads thee far from truth and clear?
For I, enthralled by thy beauty,
Turn my eyes to other things, and my heart to earth.
  For thou art fair as any child of light,
  And I, foolishly, do follow thy lead.


