Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And that vice hate with thee as a gauge doth show
Thy own love hath this treasure doth hate make,
Which yellow parchment in thy breast doth cover with pride
Thyself in thy breast doth lie in wait,
Making a disgrace where there ought to be none.
For why should my love be so strongly grieved
When my love hath such cause to grieve,
For well I know, from thy deeds,
Thyself being the grave whereon this discontent lies.
  Thou that art so strongly in love with me here
