Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
To my sightless soul, they conceal the shame.
Yet, fearing lest my soul may wander,
They grieve with subtle art, as if to say,
"See, if he walks on this plain, gracious soul."
The beauty gracing thy soul, they mourn,
And thou, in turn, grieve with subtle care,
As if to say, "This sorrow may find grace in his."
  But when he appears in glory, they mock thee,
  And with subtle care, they stroke his face with disdain.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to share this grief?
Then should I weep for thee, more than for myself,
For then I shall think of thee, and weep even more;
And then I shall heal thee, and return
Though longer then thou shouldst live.
Then can no heart for love of thee reprieve
Than that which is beset on thee from afar.
O, what a mansion for evil thoughts has made its abode
In thee, then may I praise thee even when thou art gone!
  For then I may be true, and others may be false,
 


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
Than he by fortune may hold the peace.
For, having no guardian, no form finds
Upon thyself to claim his due,
So, thou my debtor, to whom I am confined,
Cannot, will, oppress me with words, though my heart
Wants to be repaid in kind, not with presents exchanged.
  To lose him I'd be as the blind find
  Finding love, and losing myself so vile.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
