More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
To say within thine inner thoughts's core
Thy desires are desires that to thee I send.
And yet, to have mine own heart in another's hands
Was nothing short of a dream to me,
