And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
So far for love I love my life less dear
Than for love I sometime feel for surety,
For surety is much more rare in thy love.
Then why should I tallies thy worth with my grief,
When I am surety in thy heart is thine?
No love toward me then will I blunt,
Unless thou robs thy love of my will;
  Lascivious grace, in whom all ill well shows,
  Kill me with spites if thou wilt, yet we must not be foes.


Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
But thine eyes, although they see, are deceived;
They know what they look on darkly are deceived,
And for the painted lie they most approve.
They look on thee, and say
Thy face is fair, but eyes like those of slanderers;
They know not what virtue doth thy heart esteem,
To say it is born of more pleasure than truth it doth appear.
  Yet, Love, beauteous eyes, in thy heart are deceived,
  As those whose eyes are thine, in other things deemed.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Though she knows well my days are past their prime.
But why should I believe her when I see
Her falsehoods, even though she knows them to be false,
And why should I trust her when I am proved
True even in her falsified pride?
For I am dumb, and she in me
Cannot boast that I know it to be false,
Although she knows it to be false, yet I deceive
And in this she loves me, not for my sake,
