One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To give life anew to a foundered fleece,
A wild and free gift to plunder,
A thriftless crafter, in sluttish care,
Who craves no form of labor, no skill,
But, like a craven, spends all her might,
To make her worthless and bare,
A worthless mother, in sluttish pride.
  Such is her spirit, so is she;
  She lends, but takes what she wants, not finds.


