When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Though not acquainted with all the vulgar tongue;
And that she can soothe my strange sight
By paying me straight for my worth,
As if I never left her.
But why should I trust her when I am proved
True despite her deceit,
And see her more blessed than I have known?
The truth is, she loves me because I am her,
And she knows well my falseness,
Though she did not better prove it by my will.
  To lie against me she answers thus:
  She loves me because she knows well my lies.


O, call not me to justify the wrong
