One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To seek a place where it may not stray,
Yet, I, enthralled, arm myself with all
My might, to bear this mother's vexation;
But, ah, I, not tame to fortune's will,
Cannot help but lean towards the chase,
My own heart's desire, outbraiding all others.
No skill can I to discern where I should belong,
If I but belong to your love, and thus,
  Discover what love's true worth is,
  In which you and for love I find our decree.


