More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
To say within thine own deep-sunken eyes
Thy cherished love hath no claim, to mine eye.
But if it please thee, dear confidant,
As I will myself, and therein live
The lives of those that hate to see me tend.
Then do I promise, though thou me self away
