In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight it draws.
For how can I love thee save by thy inward light?
The eyes that love are prejudiced against my grace,
And hence my sin is more boldly shown,
Than by their thoughts, though they err in their rank.
Mark how one endowed with eyes for love runs
Through manifold trials and throes of despair;
Then, I believe, thy love shall in these flags see,
Even as heaven's choicest riper should bear
His sharpest offense, when heaven's truth is tried.
  Let others judge thy worth by


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Mine own love, no loving, is false,
A love-killer, in thy vices mixed.
Thou art thy own vice, and thy love
Strikes me as a vice, more vile and cruel.
Mine own love, so great, my hate
May make me forget thy name,
As vice, in thy transgressions mixed.
  But why thy name not come to pass,
  The grave hate of my soul against heaven.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To the wide world, her joy and her regret
Distilled in a mountain spring, wherefrom they come.
So too, my love, once built up like a phoenix
In every far corner of the world,
I find my loveliest remains,
Unblemished, warm, and true,
Yet, still, I fear, of time's unyielding reign.
For as the sun does chase the moon away,
My love, now whole and bright,
Cries out for you, under the sun.
  And so, I remain, in hope that time will restore


