Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And that due is thine alone,
So far as my love or thy love goes.
In this we find our difference,
Though in our nature's workings sweet love
We find sweet pains, yet love still doth grow.
Let us love with that compare,
That thou thyself in loving mayst prove
As hard to change as thou thyself art.
  Preserve thyself, be thou mine,
  As thine, so is my spirit's dove.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To seek a place where love may yet thrive,
Unyielding to the allure of false.
So I, like a vigilant maiden, seek not out
The faults concealed within the heart's core,
For love's pure light will bestow it,
In truth's domain, where it forever resides.
  In truth's domain, there is no wrong,
  And thus, I remain steadfast, caught in love's embrace.


