Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Beneath thy cold eyelids, black sin is etched.
Before they laid the musculature for thee,
Thy summer's bloom they wore, blood to keep.
The fields of sun and shrubs were thine, planted,
When summer's bounty was stolen, laid in
By cruel anger, though far away.
