Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
While hate to thy heart lives in thine own core.
Redeem thyself, dear heart, for love it doth enrich,
Give life anew to thine own, unused pleasure,
A gift to cherish thee and me tenfold,
Give us strength, to bear with such sighs,
No need for strength from thee alone.
  This thou shalt not find, if thou desire,
  A novel proof for love that still is young.


