Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Within thy own society such great might
Thy unworthy count as have not his first owners.
Two of thine own lovers, one estrang'd by nature from thee,
Constrangle one in thy breast, loyal enemy
Bethean rage by thy confounding removed, sweet heart
Of double consort from one no partner prolonged,
Bound being twice thy rivals lead.
  My love's virtue, with longer hate wait,
  Desiring what is thy due, thee doubting of times.


