I, likewise, refrain from encroaching,
While making observations of the unmatched beauty,
Finding no life beyond this earthly realm,
In other words, I remain aloof,
Aloof from life's rude, cruel, and fleeting flight.
  So, thou serene, quiet husband; in absence,
  I abide, and watch over the house.


