Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May stay with him, secure in guarantee.
So, my love, you have an audience with me,
And I, in affront, must bow
To that show of weakness and care;
To lose him, I'd give myself whole,
And for my love, I'd lose both soul and end.
  But, having heard your reasons, I no longer care
  If he lives or dies, for I am secure in thee.


