In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Enamored of thine in every vice.
For why dost thou then love what I despise,
The company of thy thoughts, entwined in love's embrace?
Oh, therefore, sweet heart, know this truth:
My love is but as a bard; it knows
What it calls upon thee to sing;
To grasp what it gazes on, it calls upon thee.
  Then, thou know, I may say with truth,
  I love thee as thou dost them adore thee.


