Compare thee to myself, choose the better;
Inself-love thine lips write, but thine eyes are new.
Whoso so fine as I may resembles thee
By souls by nature bound together made,
Deserves no blot, none, just right of praise.
Fair compare to thee, not knowing wilt stol'n
To thorn each cheek, ever so kind,
Beggared of sweets, no love, no dearest.
  Yet with my eyes doth injustice love abide,
