I'll vow myself blind, to love truth in all it touches,
And for my love to lie as fast as I think of growth,
To prevent secret feelings from weeks hence.
O, my love, swear it, and believe me not;
For thou knew'st I love thee before
That I, of this should love thee no more.
  In nothing I loved I found a true love,
  But in thy soul that love doth shape now.


Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
But thou, Love, love's illusion, do show
The bloody tenon of truth, not to my eyes;
And that, my bones, might themselves be broken
To view truth in thine eyes.
Mark how one eyes cannot grasp the beauty of another,
While seeing, but inwardly love is painted;
And in that heart, all beauty's transgression lies.
  Love, arrest thy fall, for mine eyes are still hanging,
  And hearing voices, still love's complaint.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
