Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To seek the spoil of the fledglings,
To those fair birds, which with a mournful cry
Reveal their dearest love to strangers, abandoning
The care of the child, to others' surprise.
But if you happen on this written word,
Forget the one who calls, for love runs deep,
He's your treasure, and you can claim
His love, too, in abundance, hidden in plain sight.
  In this verse, your love appears,
  And he, in turn, seems to approve.


