Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the sweet haven where it needs to be nursed.
So, too, may you be run away, unyielding,
For love's sweet scent commands swift response,
And swiftly becomes the nest where your child finds
A loving mother's sweet cry.
No harm can mar me while your love remains,
For love's sweet power will hold me,
Unyielding, and kind, forever tight.
