Generating dev sonnets for chrF scoring...
Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
To my heart's desire, black is the new red,
And all things gracious in me, be they seen,
Desiring thee, black is the only acceptable color.
So then, love, cease this torment, and grant me fairness,
As I desire thee fair, even though thou dost hate
Thine own shape, when in others' hearts it lies.
For how can I love thee when thou art hate'st,
