I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Though not acquainted with truth.
Though she may be false, yet I love her dearly,
To keep alive my notion of her worth,
Defying every blot she can lay,
Even those that I shall not live to see.
How can love so fervent believe in reviled
A lie so vile and so false,
When she knows well my wrongs I do strive?
  In truth and right, I do live quite apart,
  And to her I send this written embassage:
  I love her, for she loves me so.


