One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To avoid the likeliest of accidents
When a lone wolf, well-versed in strife,
Plods dully on ahead, no need for aid.
So, if you happen on this written phrase,
Keep your eyes open, though my heart may roam,
For love's sweet memory may still bestow
Though distance keeps us far from each other's gaze.
  Lest your true love seems false in this,
  Keep your eyes fixed, though my heart may wander.


