One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
She cries out, no longer able to rise,
The joy of birth, now with grief turned inward,
A mournful song, a vanished sight in sight.
I watch as birds, sweet birds, no longer sang,
Their songs now silenced, as the night grows long,
In sympathy, their songs become echoes,
Of what once was a joyful song, now lost in the night.
  I mourn for love that once was a bright light,
  Now bound in darkness, with others all around.


