Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And therefore, blindly, they misconstrue
The truth they so willingly give o'er.
Mark how one string, sweetheart, doth beguile
Another, more blessed, from his loving grasp;
And, all in war, one string do vie
Against all the rest, and against myself alone.
Stupid heart, why do you cling to this blemished shadow,
That you may not see the forest for the trees?
  The earth may have lost its verdant hue,
  But no man's hue is so bright that it fears no blot.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And that I might have some slighted skill
To leap from truth to falsehood as fast as I can.
But, ah, why should I believe her when I see
Her falsehoods rehearsed, her fears stoked,
And all the rest dressed as reasons why
I should not love her then?
No, let me love her with honesty,
And then she knows I was her first choice,
And that I did love her then.
  But her perjury rings so true
  That I almost straightjacket myself.


