In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of my sightless soul.
For they look on truth with marred eyes,
And in thy sins find favor in my deeds;
But heaven in thy creation did decree
That in thy endless play they should see right,
Not accepting of shadows thy deeds contain.
  For nothing 'tis heaven in thy creation that doth decree,
  But thy deeds, being bad, being sweet, they measure evil.


