Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May claim my equal;
So, by what force dost thou detain me,
My dear love, and for this cause detainest
My dagger, which cannot harm him in this plight.
O, what a haven for vice has made its nest
In thee, wherein beauty's veil conceals each vice,
Where darkness hides behind a sunlit crest,
And sins are cloaked by the guise of sacrifice!
  Take heed, dear heart, of this seductive mask;
  The sweetest touch corrupts the heart's most precious treasure.


