Give that heart to my mistress' slave?
  Shew her eyes, and yet they see not thee;
  They look, but the heart still doth deceive.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Though she knows well my days are past their prime.
But why should she rely
On men's memories, so false a guide?
They are better at recalling things they know well,
And I, they less prone to fall for traps planted there.
They see farther than I do, and that's why they're so slow,
Of course, I'm slow to trust in things I've been told.
  And so they believe her, despite their worth,
  In their fond belief, I end up with them.


