Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the place where it grew.
So you, my lovely, will find love again,
More blessed than before, more strong,
And tender love, more then gentle sighs,
Will bear your weight, and still cry:
"Graceful, caring, and true"
In love's own book, where every line is writ,
