So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit by thy part.
O, let me suffer, being at thy beck,
Th' imprisoned absence of my liberty,
And patience, tame to sufferance, bide each check
Without accusing thee of injury.
Be where thou wishest, thy charter so great
That thou thyself dost whatever thy charter doth compel,
Though thou art not obliged to compel my will,
By thy own merit alone making me suffer.
  Such is my love, to suffer no wrong,
  That I an accessary will be happy to see.


