So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit by thee and for my life.
But do not so. I love him as is due;
Thyself so strongly committed, that I will not change
My mind, although he may change it with thee.
Love him as I shall thee, for I love him that way,
And he, in like plight, is forced to yield
To my will, though I will not change my state.
  So, I be still, though he live and die;
  Even so, my love is thine and him thine.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
When ten times happier me than thou canst bear,
Thy wish being more than enough to make me live.
Ten times thy love, if ten of them were my will,
I should be left alone, my dear one;
But being forego'd, I have recourse made,
And that love, which so foully touched thee,
Is this, that love which in thy breast doth live.
  This love is so strong, that it bends
  To every kiss, each touch, with each injury.


