Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet in their seeing, thine eyes are deceived.
Why should my eyes be false, seeing so great a face,
When I in thy bosom's depth see the earth covered,
And in thy shadow's place, the sun?
Though they may not see the world, yet, by thy shadow,
They know thy shadow well, and thy fair appearance show
How thy shadow on thine bosom doth grow.
  And yet, Love, what a beauty dost thou make
  Out of thy shadow's form, which thou thyself dost deceive.


