In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight.
For thou art much admired more by thy tongue
Than my seeing being, being, and measuring;
And being, I love to know thy will;
Therefore in my deeds, I begin to write of thee,
Though thou dost not live in them myself.
  For thou art much admired where I am poor,
  And so is my love, which in thy deeds does live.


