Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
For to thy own soul I give all my might,
And for myself to love thee even so.
That is my love, and that is my will,
Two souls entwined in love's sweet table.
Yet one cannot live without the other,
For that which thou dost love dost live is thy self.
  Thus then my love, though mine own heart be untrue,
  By thy love I am thyself deceived.


