In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight it draws.
For if my eyes be marred, thy heart's delight
In right is thy inward flame kindled;
If my eyes be false, thy love's sweet deceit
Enshrouds in mist and shadows wherever it goes.
How can my heart believe in thee when it sees
Its own worth is marred by thy deeds,
Suff'ring thy sweet name, thy sweet name for which it hates?
  Refrain from calling me to account,
  For I am the sanctuary where thou shalt find thy sweet peace.


