Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To give full honor to her love, which leaps and sings;
But Lo, I, kept from thee, depart,
My life and love untouched, with fear bound,
For in my stead, she waits, unbent.
Her heart is moved, though her lungs are full,
By pity, and my love, by delight,
Gathers tears, and waits, unbent;
Then, if the pain should be my love's gain,
Then she, my heart, and I become one,
In love's sweet symphony, where love's sweet notes meet.
