And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
O, swear, be the tenth muse, ten times more in worth,
Than thy poets' ten plays on that score.
Let those sacred tens remain ten,
Or at least ten times more, be them lords of that space.
If thou survive my well-contented day
When that blessed sound my verse shall expound,
Then thank not me for praises I sing,
But let those poor rude lines where I did strive
Proceed where my fair subject lie.
  For thou art thy poet, and I am thy respect,
  And both together do thee proud.


Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And therefore with a kind of disdain,
They look into the beauty of thy mind.
