So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit from thy love even more.
But, do not so. I love him still, though he hath changed,
Like a widowed spirit, yet in my breast
Thyself I feel so strongly bound,
That I in him as well as him doth live.
That is why I bring him in my mind,
To think on thee, and on thy love,
That in my breast doth lie a grave mistake.
  For thee, dear heart, I so love him,
  That thou mayst take him hence, when thou wilt.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
To say within thine own deep-sunken eyes
Thy self thou no longer canst breathe;
To others' wills, thy sweet argument
