  Kill me, then, and I'll understand
  That no hatred toward thee remains, though thou art dead.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the place where the fleece lies,
In safety of her babe's heart.
So you, like a mother goose, with care
Of her small clutch, remain near,
Hungry for your child's warmth, and keep
Your gaze steady, though motionless, lest
The spoil of your delight turns sour.
Whoso restrains you, let them find rest,
No longer can you frantically look
For the one you love, in joy or pain.
