So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit by thy service;
And, for myself, a better state
Than that which on thy humor doth depend.
Look what is best, that best I wish in him.
That is, him that allows my love to die.
Then let him be executor of my will,
Since I thee only gain by his will,
And he that receives my riches will be happy.
  Then let him be absent from my sight,
  Being at thy beck, with others all around.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
To leave thee as the just deserts grant
Thou deserv'st alone, to bear thy defect.
I will lend thee virtue, yet on thine own desert
Thyself would be guilty, were it not thy will
To be so kind, to be so kind.
I will lend thee virtue, be it thy will or me
To be thy debtor, that to thee I do owe;
Thus, thou mayst be surety my love will be
By my behavior, not by my will.
  To be so kind, to be so kind
