And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit by thy service.
This I do not do upon thy tongue,
For I haply think on thee, and so should he,
Although he hath no part in love's design.
That he may keep my love is my claim,
And so is my poor mistress' heart,
One of many, all in one,
From whom he will derive a great gain.
  She may keep him, but not me,
  For I must be the tenth, and he the tenth.


