So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May benefit by thy tie.
That is why I have recourse to thee,
For I must not be dumb in knowing thy will,
For I serially preposterously be dumb,
Knowing thy will, knowing thy doubles are thine,
And in so dumb a mind, I impair
Thy self, to benefit myself here and there.
  For thee, I am dumb, and he is strong,
  In so much dumber I impair thine own soul.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
