Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
To say within thine own deep-sunken eyes
Thy cherished love outshines every vice,
Even to the edge of base crime.
That she woos thee, I woe, yet have mercy,
For I must be base, and so slight
As strangers to thy sweet crime call.
I must be willing, even to be thy debtor,
To suffer thy liberty, though thou dost compel
Myself to be thou.
