Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet in thy picture dost thou seem so blind
To believe in things that thou dost deceive.
Whence dost thou derive this blindness, that thou mayst
See, when thou no form of thee dost show?
To tell the truth of a lie doth thy advantage give,
Which can make thee blind if thou thyself be untrue.
  For to thyself thy picture dost give,
  And to thyself thy truth dost give.


