Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet in eyes dost deceive, and therein appear
The most precious of all thy wiggards.
They look on thee through their haze,
And like to the lily dost thou stick,
Whilst others all their parts of thee do mock their sight.
Then on thy show thy truth with outward guise,
For thine eyes thy true grace dost deceive,
And thy given name confounds,
And all things turns to make things right.
  But do thy worst to steal what is thine,
  Since to thine eyes thy gift confeth.


