If thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Give me the strength, to bear thy whimsical lead,
The captive's absence in thy liberty's cell,
With forbearance, I'll endure, each pause and thread,
Without reproach, thy freedom's shifting sort.
Roam where thou desireth, thy right so immense,
That thou thyself may grant time's own boon,
In thine hands, lies pardon, far and wide,
By my will, I'm bound, to suffer no complaint.
  I'll wait, though torment, be the companion of waiting,
  If thy unworthiness hath wrought my thread.


Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet, darkly, they see through
The sun's lens, and see in its reflection how it doth appear.
The first-sighted eyes, in their gazing,
Are anchored in a cove where hearts take flight;
Yet, Love, they glimpse what shallowest sight can hold,
The sun, though it doth first appear,
To thy picture's worth, what it doth say.
  If thyself should eyes be deceived,
  The first-sighted eyes should look into thy mind.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
But that I should scorn to trust her, knowing her lies,
To keep alive the notion of my youth,
Unsuspecting of life's deceitful arts.
Thus, she believes me gullible, unwise,
Though she knows full well my days are fleeting,
I play along, her falsehoods I endure,
And in this act, truth on both sides hides.
But why does she not admit her wrong?
And why do I not confess my age?
  Love's most endearing trait is pretense,
  And age in love dislikes the telling of years.


