Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As shadows flee before the dawn has broken,
And beauty fades before the morning light.
For thy sweet love I've kept so close,
As interestor to the quest of graves,
Whereas thou desireth, thy heart's desire.
Thou art as tyrannous, murd'rous, and to me,
As I regard thy worth, thy virtue, thy faithfulness.
For thou art the treasure of my heart's treasure,
