Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
In sympathy, tearing my world apart.
Forget me, my heart, once I have left this place,
For I see the truth with thy eyes,
And know thy heart's desire, too,
To part from me, as thou dost thine own part.
So, I guess, by this, thou know'st
Time's cruel hand, with thee, I must part,
And do what thou desire, swift-changing Time's own part.
  This part I do, that for thee,
  That thou mayst part, and I am a part.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
