Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Basking in Death's eternal, warming grace.
This scene, so often, transcends the bounds of old,
Unyielding to the ravages of Time's relentless chase;
Now, in this realm where naught is truly new,
Only reused, refashioned from the old,
An insignificant fault, no more, by bards designed.
  Let those who bask in this eternal fire,
  Shall find their names in verse, not in stars.


