One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To work her hands when body's work's expired.
For fear of ill fortune's false adulterate eyes
Give salutation to my love, Ah, sweet thief of time!
They look kindly on my sorrow,
And mock my dire state with mock sweet spite,
Then usefully of their reproof's might.
