Those lips that Love's own hand did make
Breathed forth the sound that said "I hate"
To me that languished for her sake;
To lips that Love's own touch had graced
With words of hearts to contradict,
I would say "I hate" and "I love"
To those who would never understand my care.
O, what a sanctuary for love of sighs
We call upon thee, our hearts entwined in love's sweet symphony,
Where heaven's ornaments and earth entwine
In splendid tapestry of loved-filled days.
  Let those who bask in love's sweet power,
  Seek to ensnare hearts with false and proud compare.


Poor soul, the center of my sinful earth,
Pressed with these rebel powers that thee array,
