Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Gentle on my sorrow, they weep,
As compassion's ally, in every woe,
I think my eyes best, in love's sweet pleasure.
Yet, as they view me, in their haze,
Their eyes, a twisted mirror reflecting thy cares,
At thy fair face, no painter's art could seize,
To feel the beauty of thy friend, so gazed on now,
Now seize the instant, to rejuvenate.
  Yet, as they view, their eyes, in discord,
  The sun, though masked, still burns with ardent flame.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
