And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine;
For, having him, it is thine alone,
My loss would be my gain.
The loss of thee, my self-esteem so high,
Would be my gain, and mine own gain,
For bending on thy love, the shallowest help.
