For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to share this grief?
It is the home of love and guilt,
Which in its chaotic world I find my solace
And in my madness, I'm torn by its sweet deceit.
My heart, it knows
Imprison my sin in its unyielding breast,
