Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Childless, who cry out, unheard;
I, the lone bard, run swiftly to your aid,
Your child, loved and still seeking your guidance fair.
Yet, if you find
Your hope, your heart's desire, do turn around,
Embrace me, soothe me, be the mother I need,
And I shall pray for your success, unbound.
