Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And sense the bitterness that slaves?
Why should they marvel at what they see,
Beated anew, as never before?
Why should their eyes most delight now
By looking on darkness of the world?
Why should they grieve at the sight of beauty's glare,
