In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Whilst my eye hath played the painter and hath stelled,
Thy soul hath drawn thy picture in table of sight,
And the 'tis the world's fresh expression of our desire
That I view therein with fidelity;
But when my eye is out of heaven,
Mine eye hath played the painter and hath stelled thee,
And hath stelled thee in the frame of men.
  Take heed, dear heart, of this painted deceit;
  For thee it is thine to my art which eyes partake.


