Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
As I all other in all things lovely,
Finding fault in one thing expressing,
Th' own faults proved more base in seeming.
For there can live no hatred in thine eye;
Therefore in that I cannot know thy change.
O, what a gulf exists between us,
To though the years may divide.
Yet, love, increase thyself with gentle love,
