Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To his side, where he is driven.
The one who possesses his energy and is not half so king,
The one who possesses his spare, and still has journeyed on alone.
So I, by fortune's dearest spite made lame,
Do call upon thy gifts, and borrow from thy body's strength,
To prove what beauty lies in me.
  Teary of fortune's choicest boon,
  Tattered and stilled, I this call upon thy heart.


