When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And in that service, heaven's malice hid.
But not for this my heart she imparts,
And with sweet lies, I comfort my silence with gentle care;
So thou suborned informer, sweet falsehoods
And in thy darkest corners sing my vows.
Who hath taught thee how to feign trustfulness
To swear against me, day by day,
And to thyself at least in thy darkest corners lend;
  For beauty's truth in thy darkest corners doth lend,
  As dark as any shield she can devise.


