Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
So I, by heaven's dearest spite made lame
Find my heart's true love, and in thy heart's deep well I know.
For thou art fair as any child of light,
Though not as stars, whose brilliance I can't see;
But from heaven's graces graces I despise,
Although in their eyes my judgment thoth prepare the heart's array.
  If thou wouldst but pause, and let me be dumb,
  I'd not steal that honor from thy brow.


