It's better to be receives reproach of being,
And ruined love, when it's new?
  For thy sweet virtue hath wrought this huge crime,
  That in thy darkness my deeds must be shown.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To share in love's eternal cause.
The summer's flower charms summer's soul,
Existing for itself, it only reflects his love's tender care,
And gained a pearl, by Love's own fire.
But if this bloom encounters vilest plight,
The lowliest weed may rise to its stature,
To mar the bloom of its revered source.
  For purest things, by deeds defiled, turn vile,
  Lilies that fester stink worse than the soil.


