Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As if in sympathy, they seem blind.
I cannot frown upon thy sorrow's endless flow,
Nor find the loss of right to me,
Nor canst thou share in secret pains,
Unless you leave its disgrace.
I cannot more deeply than sorrow's tide,
Nor canst thou share in love's boundless ocean,
When others petty griefs have played their bitter part,
