Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Adorned with black to comfort me, causing
My heart to weep for loss, and bewail
My misery in black as dead somber long.
But now my heart hath all new wrath laid,
Adorned with news of thy distress,
It looms against the sight of the night,
And doth this torment me more:
  For thoughts of thy crime doth stain,
  And this, more than the others, doth find me doth sully, write me dead.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And leave my soul to cry within
The throes of another's cruel, proud breast?
I will not complain, nor inquire why,
The world's set in such a woe, if it please,
