Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
Thy wantonness may claim the prey. Lo, Love, where are you now,
Save in the withthed fortress of my breast,
From whence dost thou leave the place, save
By the bastard ebb and flow? Still, have the dearest love,
Whate'er choice thou but vote within,
Whate'er punishment thou but withstand,
Either up or down, do your worst.
  I should like to have life ere this,
