Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of its restless flight, so does my poor Gilda
Carry my love, by Mom's side, by her breast
Where it doth nest, as if it were a child,
Till at last it yield, at rest, to death,
Returning with sweet report, from doom's distant shore.
