Deprived of my just deserts,
I be a cruel mistress, thrice my debtor.
I love thee through my own wretchedness,
So I'll pay that myself one price,
Although he owes me ten thousand for my part.
  Just so, love; yet hate me so,
  For I cannot be guilty of such a crime.


