I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Still clinging to beauty's truth, unconfined.
That she might be false, and I be true,
Two lies with two souls entwined,
Love and Lies, now living as one,
Three very different things, but one in love's sweet role.
Believe not, though she swears, that she is made of stars,
Whilst in reality she is but a mortal shell,
Three little moments stretched out over countless eons,
Three layers of falsehood gone by,
Three flows of love, now distilled,
A cure for all ailments that a lover fears.
 


