Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
The mother, in chide, checking all off,
Calls out to her reborn child, her old mate,
And says with a sigh:
"Mamma, you have changed your mind,
And given yourself away."
The maiden mother, distraught, stands there, speechless,
Then to the chase, her spirit broke,
And in reproof she cries:
"Mamma, you had better things planned
For yourself, child of mine,
Plundered by chance, your beauty for me,
Or else, by fortune's dearest spite, you'll die."


