I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
If I should task her with learning my rhyme.
Thus, to be obsequious in her heart
And to true love excuse her errors,
I bide her whims like a thrifty pawn
And hope she will buy what worths I bring.
Although, often in my words she lies,
Yet, in them I find my heart's ache,
And so, believe me, I am in love with her.
  This love is such, to swear and to live,
  For she knows well my life's hinge depends.


