And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May seize the liberty of that will.
Such a cathartic niggard will be found
In one so fond upon the subject of his love,
To give away all that he has, more than double
The cost of a few groans and sighs.
Such a fool is love, it knows
Even that a true heart's high design
Hath been stol'n from the start, and is now
