Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Creeping softly towards the darkness covered.
They look into the depth of thy heart,
And thereupon their faces take command,
Chasing shadows from thy path they're swift.
But why should I reproach them for fading?
My lips, which would sing a tear,
At their own hearts' heavy toll be.
To be so mingled with sorrow hath my heart been
Since first I saw thy face;
Yet to black eyes' torment I'm about to rise.
  In torment I'll face this new-appearing sorrow,
  And thank the eyes for their love, which


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to share that fate?
It wrests me from myself, your tyrant hold
