So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine increase.
For this purpose entering I must not surprise thee,
For thou art in no worthiness of any,
And he that is so, though he be thine,
Is but his prospect thrown off, so should I be.
Therefore will I so count my own want,
Being under thy control,
Thyself I'll despise, to whom thou art so kind.
Mark how one poor rose looks on thee,
With eyes that love themselves, lessing his own;
So will I scorn to change my state with thee.
