Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Or to thy dark deeds do offer light,
As to thy fair looks tribute are due.
For to thy dark deeds do I bring
A tribute, and in that merit live.
But why thy sins do I not allude,
Although thou art all my offences charged?
Since all my faults are so charged,
And yet thy blessed allure still rivals
At least as far as the eye can see.
  For sweet grace do I in that love call,
  Where faults have nothing to complain.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the chase, wherewith it's sought, her husbandry
With her babe is resumed, with gentle ease it runs.
So you, in your discreet chase,
Child of mine, tendered my love,
And therefore, having no end in view,
Thou, that child, remaining still, wilt prove none.
For to thee I send this written embassage:
"Thou child of mine, which I love so deeply,
