Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
She keeps her gaze steady, the sun in her hand it sets;
Nothing moved by Time's fanatics can now be caught,
Or speed him from place to place.
From the moment when he takes his stand,
To rove and tell tales of antique days,
No pen has all their ancient grace set,
Or stretched to every bound being.
He can tell the tale of yore,
Yet lives no more to tell it;
He walks past and past alone,
Lost in thoughts of thee, his heart it is.
  Yet, like the sun, he shall endure,


