O, call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
Show me no hostility in thy cheer,
 but rather a kind of thankfulness
For sore subjects require gentle soothing.
I will be kinder to thy sorrow
Than thou mayst command the winds to do favors;
And in that goodness even so as thou art kind
I see a benefit, for thy wrongs well prove
Thy sweet heart's stronger, stronger being to me.
Thou canst not vex me with inconstant mind,
