Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And, stopped there, they believe it not.
My eyes, ensnared, no vision can seize,
And yet to thy rosy lips and to thy cheeks touched
The basest art may claim victory.
Thy charm lies in this, that mine eyes may see
And to thy distillation look,
Making memories of love that long to have.
  All days are beauties till thou thyself arise,
  And nights are beauties till thou thyself depart.


