Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As appendix to a sick body;
Thou hath given thyself another impression,
And next to me a kind of panel
To that which I by inclination hated.
How much more doth sorrow grieve me when I think on thee,
Than sufferance of a first impression's offender;
That sin which gives thee so much grace doth equip
And Tie up all tight with usurpation's knot.
