Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
She keeps pace with those who fly in flocks,
Her gilded ornament, a precious guide,
In tender touch, their path is led,
By her joy, their course is set, and they turn.
Mad in pursuit, they run after wind,
In joy's fullness, they grasp the breeze,
Then, come to a halt, as the true
Bestows its value, on whom it grew.
  A foolish child, chasing hope,
  Leaving mothers to their fates.


