And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May have victor's prize, converted from dross to gain;
For that love hath wrought upon my heart
That it may prevail against myself
Toil for thee, against myself I'll be defeated
In this love, toil and fear have I found
