When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And give me some new learning to engage
When I am old men themselves.
But why does she not say so,
When she knows full well my days are fleeting?
And why do I not claim my freedom
When I am in the best of shape,
Of my age, by continual news?
For love's sweet veil does not show
The years, though the sun is black,
And beauty fades, burnt and lame,
Like the dyer's hand, dyed by its own career.
  So I swing back and forth, both grieved and happy,
