Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And how to find it, with eyes this dumb,
Doubting the vision of thy treasure.
Thou sly Deceiver, Love, what hold dost thou
On my heart, that it may see what lies in thee?
No sway, I suppose, my heart's inclination bewined
On thine every question, its truth determined.
