Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Desiring this heart to suffer, through sorrow's assault.
Yet thou hast passed this hell, and skillfully gone
Beyond the reach of lame despair;
Yet I, envious, won't be grieved at all,
Unless this misfortune grant thee far auspicious days.
  Then shall I feel pity, and then impart
  A lesson learned in this hell.


