Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine can live
By thyself's, not to commocate with thee.
So I have sworn thee fair, and told my story,
That thou dost love him for my love's reprieve,
And therefore have I recourse where my life is threatened.
Thy looking glass, thy picture displayed,
Conceals thy truth quite, softening its tone;
A blessed lie, that thy glass shows thee how
To make one twain with two stones changed;
  Such lies are against thy nature's design,
  To cherish what thou dost withhold.


