When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And so my disgrace springs from my love's deceit.
But why does she not boast of this growing age?
And why do I not brace against time's cruel scythe,
When my days are numbered and her beauty ends?
For love's sweet habit is to feign trust,
And age in love dislikes the telling of years.
  So, perfected love remains in operation,
  Unbettered, though men come and go.


