Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To wherever it is that it may run.
But if the father, busy as a teachest in his swell,
Holds still the child's foot in his lap,
The tyrants' anger is done,
And the proud mother, proud as an orphan,
Plods her sake upon the willing thread.
So, if you, my little one, happen on this written word,
Forget the one who did keep you so dear,
For love is more enduring than lose.
  So, if you happen on this written word,
  You've but lost your chance.


