So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may obtain
By thy injurious spirit's power.
I have detailed how thy dear merit may be
Entwined with benefit, how to make him grow
Through the ties of thy friendship and trust;
Yet advised him to break free
Because I was certain of his fairness;
He hath since then added me as collateral,
To a surety placed even there.
  Since he hath done this, have I no more shall doubt
  But that my share is thy own, single.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And yet I cannot forbear, see?
To some unclean impurity I bring in debate,
But I in thy canker balls will live.
The drops of thy fragrant love are everywhere,
And in my love's veins thou hast your vengeance.
I may not escape thy harshness,
Nor find the delight of that gallant hobgoblin,
Whose tender touch brings accusation after accusation.
  But do thy worst, O certifiable tyrant,
  And I the farther off, behold thy pleasure.


