Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the chase, the capture, and bring them back home.
So I, made weary from thy care,
Should hurry to my bed, turn around,
And return, even though the world did run very fast,
No horse with my desire could turn a tiring fast.
No horse could match my desire,
And, perfected love, would have my companion
Matching his might, through the strongest force.
Love for love's sake shall excuse my bareness:
  "Since from thee going he went willful slow,
  My love shall hasten, granting him reprieve."


