Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To chase that which she best knows no where.
So I, made poor and lame, must attend
The sweet and great events of my friend's life,
Who, full of health, now flourishing and happy,
Cries out for mercy, being made lame,
No longer able to grasp what
He wants, being sick of life.
  Thus, like a lambs, scarred and mudded,
  By carelessly losing him who calls me well.


