So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may retain
His dear-purchased right, which for myself I'll not repossess.
Thus, thou cunning slanderer; a true heart
Shines brightest when beset by darkest art;
And for myself mine own worthiness
Is most in thy control, being lent
By that sweet thief who steals me away.
  Let him, so rich, languish who concedes
  The right of others to hold what he doth own.


