When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And play the laudary role of gullible plea,
Wounded along the path of truth we both fear.
Yet, she knows full well my days are fleeting,
And in her deceit she finds such charm,
That she carries me along, through
The furious beating of this uncertain path.
  So, she thinks me gullible, unwise,
  To play along with her, though she knows full well my days are numbered.


O, call not me to justify the wrong
