Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
So I, being made of more stone,
Cease this selfish chase, and soothe
My own heart, made more strong by desire;
Let love's own sweet purpose fill my tomb,
Unmoved by the quick expense or brave punishment.
O, let me, true in love, think this truth:
My heart is boundless, and so is my treasure,
So is my love's golden guarantee,
Which in its honesty I'll prove.
  Let me love thee, as thou dost them adore,
  Not tallying ranks with choirs.


