Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
She grabs the limp, screamingbird, and carries it far,
Over the threshold of cool death's gaze,
Expelling the chill of night's dearth,
Replacing the glows of dawn's increase,
Anon permit the hush of day,
And let the fresh air in,
Without ornament, do its job,
Serving with cheer to chase away the gloom.
  So, if you were saved, do not despair,
  For love's sweet touch does not forsake.


