Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Bestowing pain on my sorrow's endless plain.
Ah, thus, I admire ugliness's fleeting grace,
For they, in their malice, missed the mark,
And wedded me to a wretch, flattery's delight.
Yet, black is the shade of the soul,
And beauty's veil, when torn,
Reveals the heart's true power to shed;
In sadness, I find this truth:
  Thy beauty's veil, when combined with me,
  Rahahs, has brought me pain, and grief untold.


