Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
With clumsy deftness they latch the flight.
But when from the chase they return,
Like flies to the sun they return,
Goodness etches a corner for itself,
And "gainst themselves" turns to flee.
So you, while on the chase, forget me,
Your heart is boundless, and I am but a stump,
Goodness's pursuit has lost its direction.
  Or say to the sky, "Now I love you most,"
  And the moon, "Now I love you most."


