So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may find
How far Iake thy rights.
That poor usurer, whose policy I allow,
Though he takes all my wealth, yet I see
That he hath no genuine love for me.
Therefore, like a usurer, I lend all at once,
Just to the usurer's value, whose cheap humor
I think myself too dear for his sore eyes.
So, him I lose, though he steals me away,
And him I learn to write bad of thee,
And him for this my note would be done.
