Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch move,
She watches him alone, tender-hearted, within,
While her enamored lover is got together,
Their murmurs are drawn within her tranquil soul,
And in surcease, she has fortune to await.
So close is my remembrance, that his blessed renown
Is enthralled in mine as true seers theresee.
O, what does my lore show, that escapes my praise?
No songs or other show can ever dim the splendor of thy golden name,
Revived, ever so briefly, thronged forth.
