Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To catch him and bring him back and hug him,
As if in love, not to break him again,
Or run him far and use a different womb to breed.
It's not true love, true, it's not the same;
We cherish him, or she, or both, cherish
Ourselves so dear, that we're willing to let go
Of one who's good, and to keep another.
  This mother, so selfish, does none
  Reward him, or him give nothing but shame and disgrace.


