When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
And by others unversed swear I am learned.
So she thinks me naive yet I have learned to read
The captivating form in which she stares,
To love me I refashion her rage so bright
That in my head she rotates as I turn around,
Gazing on those same eyes she spake,
An eye that knows no hidden cue.
Now all her might brings forth but needs my lie,
And yet her eyes have kept their gloss in flawless light,
For true love's sweet sense tells the story of wings,
A compass that points true even when gazes depart.


