Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thy precious smile made mourners want to rush
To the graves where thou art despised of men.
Mourners therefore bring thy shadow here
To vexation me with blackest black of night,
Making sly shadows appear bright on thee,
Adorning thee with women's false allure.
Thou my torment is not mine alone,
Nor is it my poor heart's issue that accounts
For thy gentle atmosphere all men praise.
  This blame they confineeth not in my love
  But in thy allure, which I think is but thy wardrobe.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
