So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may see
That she hath, though not heavenly, borrowed this great part
For sacred mine own dear dearest will;
That she doth on this contingent doom choose,
Holding me day and night, brief to show me truth;
Then why in us herein such distress dare
Sometime with this dearth she raise,
When satisfaction of such overthrow lies?
  O, blame me not then, when thou wilt crown me king;
  As thou mayst suffer I to suffer still.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And therein lie proud defenses hid.
When wouldst thou wilt make war upon my life
