Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
Yet rightly judge that it beauteous lack
To give mine eyes grace even to look on thee
Which to look on cannot afford the pleasure they see.
For straight mine own good looking therein doth lie,
The fairest object in view all naked is mine;
