That every alien tongue and every idle look
Spare me from myself's cold eye.
  For thee, my dear, time's tyrant keeps
  In likeness of my affections there ever


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Much as when our fair was first wrought,
Like fairest fruits to the eye in love.
The summer's pleasure or winter's shade
