Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
As if by some instinct she knew the run of things;
For how else are these swift messengers sent,
Their curtailing tamely their way,
When the bark of winter hath passed away?
How can most true intelligence now make light
To probe into some new wave or somber rage
Of ceaseless waiting, all naked, bare,
Lags behind the winter's bane and moan?
  Our spies, indeed, much advance in quest of thee,
  And yet, even in their gazes, thy image remains unknown.


