Then take heed, dear heart, of this deceit;
It blinds the mind, and dulls the bone;
It hardens the heart, and dulls the eye;
It swells the breast, and robs the joy;
It stings the fiercest fever, and fairestolds
Thy virtuous virtues, in safety concealed.
  Beware, sweet heart, of this too;
  A poisoned vial, thou must purge.


