That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
Yet what most doth beauty shape and make it blind.
For if it be true, and I am blind lead,
To make my eyes this large wonder why
My heart does love it so.
Thence come it that my rich glass doth shine
Even in the darkest night,
When in the day my eyes bewitched look;
In sleep a king's view,
As sweet by chance my love's day doth appear.
  Since saucy kingly days are crowned
  With all things lovely that heaven for love doth create.


