In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Desiring thine every single note.
Mine eyes in thee all groan,
Thy heart in them all breathes;
And in thy breast is discovered
Some small flower of ill.
For whether beauty, birth, or riches adore,
The most precious ornament doth beauty discard,
And in thy very being lies
Wherewith it doth deign to show.
  This told, she sighs; but then
  The least of love to thine ears doth take.


