Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
So I, with love's caution, ran to my door,
Silently posting my love's gentle quest,
When hands from my side would scarcely cease.
The baby, so unwooed, and still so hard,
With my heart's desire, answered my lady's call,
Making all haste for its bed,
At the window, where its presence would make itself known.
The window, bright as morning dew,
Hidden from its sight, like a luminous bowl,
But inside, a different story emerges,
A love-story waiting to be.
