Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
In tattered bond, to pity me,
As accomplices to torture me with extreme scorn.
Yet, as I regard thy woe, I sigh,
And with such compassion, I nod,
As pity's conquered hatred, I retreat.
For why should I grieve at thy heart, so crushed,
When I, so much more afflicted, feel
The sweetness of thy sweet sorrow, so kind?
  Oh, let me embrace thy darkness, and share,
  The boon of losing sight of thee.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind
Another soul to share this pain?
Another's heart may share this grief,
Yet lives in blissful ignorance.
Canst thou then claim I suffered in silence?
When thou, so deeply grieved, does speak
Even now that thou shalt be razed?
What merit do I see in me, so fine,
So blessed and so zealous in duty?
Yet, virtue's most precious treasure, veiled in mire,
  doth lie buried with thee, at bay.
  So, happy I, that heart which makes my heart so bitter.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May live like a second self, having sold his self away.
But what's so blessed-fair that fears no blot?
So blessed are those whose worth do measure,
And he whose goodness hath in himself be certed.
Then how, I say, couldst thou then forswear love,
Knowing thy sweet love was false, so torn?
Pity me, then, and I assure thee this:
Thy love knows no need to fear,
Though in thy deeds thou mayst show a part.
  But what's so blessed-fair that fears no blot?
