Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
And had I not vouchsafe her grand deserts,
A bett'ring gift, in me could not make the grade.
Yet her will, if ever she had that will,
A wise woman would her blessings sufficed,
And thrice happier, lived in her stead.
Th' account of mine the inferior keeps,
I am sure I am not in that store.
Therefore, gentle forsworn, I'll ne'er more swear
Than thou, to whom thy sweet love doth belong.
  To give her parting is to give full to thee,
