So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may possess
That freedom which thou dost withhold.
For to thee I so belong,
Granting no preference, why should I claim
More of thee than thy sweet self doth deem?
What reason will my poor lover give
When thou thyself dost raise a title to count
And make him swear by thy love, so great?
Then should I thrust him into this breach,
To dry the stain with a better stead;
  And revenge myself on him for all I do.
  But think on this, my love; he loves thee so.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
