Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And, churls, can you believe that you know nought
But what your husband's face bears, even down to the bone?
If he hath by chance or I by fate
fell into a vile sleep,
I blame him not, being blind,
Since that his face hath put on a show
To darken my loved's complexion with a beauteousness.
Is it not sin, being blind,
That says in my heart is darkness?
Beauteousness hath annexed to thy face,
And sin by thee remains unpunished,
