Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And I must confess that love is not love
To sin's and unrighteous dove.
For to make my love lawful,
I must repent my sins beyond the reach of sour glance,
And in that time appear
To be truly yours, through love's sweet test.
So, love, be as thy shade; I may not profess,
Lest my guilt should do thee shame,
Nor thee from my sight thence suffer'st.
  Graceful is love, and thus to be chased;
  If sweet love turns sour, the taint'st.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
So you, upon my love's departure, must be twice careful,
And both for me and for myself remain
Each by the other's care;
That you may do what thou wilt do, thou art my care,
And I shall cherish thee, to keep
The semblance of my husband's heart.
In matters of vast capacity, I shall not be
Harsh, but stern;
For I impair not beauty, granting
The due due to thee.
  By the nature of your care, I must be gentle,
  Not blame thy pleasure, whatever its dictating.


