Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As darkened by mourning, they weep,
In sympathy, tearing my world apart.
Yet, I, a sympathizer, do turn my gaze to thee,
For I see the pain in thy heart's search,
And in thy eyes, a tender care,
As needy souls resemble the rich,
Crying out for their beloved.
