So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May claim thy deed, containing words of more worth
Than what I have writ.
For to such a one shall my deed be
Bound, the subject of love,
Which for that purpose alone doth belong
To thee, my dear friend.
Thus, thou art my slave, though I do move
Thyself away, so that thou art made my wife,
And I, lame, must live, aware
That I must live, like a drush, each day
For thy love, and for myself to keep.
