In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Embracing all those things pure and ill.
In my judgment, thou fair youth, lovely friend,
When I depart from thee,
Dost share with me the wiles of the old,
Who ravished thee with their flames even so
As I by thy virtues stirred;
And for their theft, I pay the owe,
Bearing the pain, though mutual disgrace.
  But if they know their faces are fairest,
  And beauty's false glass shows what true love looks like.


