Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And I, in turn, abhorrence,
Cultivate mercy, in thy heart's core.
Such civil war is in my love born,
That, for thy sake, I will fight,
And aid thy separation, bid my friend cease.
  Such a claim is made, worth a fight,
  To grant what is owed, by my love assailed.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her nest's girth, where it may be seen
And lifted up on high to dry;
So I, made so good a catch, take all my care
Of my own dear-purchased right,
Which is my own health, to which thou hast paid
Thy gift, now my sickness;
Then, all in one, one pleasing deed
From many to one, becomes my health;
  Then in action, by fate's hand made,
  I am cured, and the whip's race is done.


