O, call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
Give not a needy jewel to a beauteous boon.
If thou wilt claim my absence is my grief
And need'st a thousand groans to repair,
I dare not blame thy cowardness;
Give me leave to repair
The injury birthed by thy unkindness;
No need for blame thy trespass hides
When thou thyself dost wrong the very thing
That mak'st thyself so vile a prime.
  In forgiving thy sins, thou my sweet self dost give
  My whole being to thee, all full with hate.


Be wise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words expresswise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express
My deepest sense, the breadth and depth of my soul's nurture.
If I could compare thee to a winter's calm?
Behold how one string, a loving partner to another,
Each by the other is stirred in mutual dance,
Resembling a sire who with his offspring does consort,
And a mother, all in one, one melodious note do sing;
  Whose unvoiced song, many and one,
  Sings thus to thee: "In isolation, thou shalt be undone."


In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Him in love with thy ideas and thy brow.
For there can live no hatred in thine eyes,
For that is within thine own soul to acknowledge;
Therefore in thy sight there is no guilt,
Though in thy soul's possession thou mysterious boon.
In silence, thy virtue lies so great,
That in thy acts thou each for thyself obtains
The glory which thy deeds would have If thou wouldst but speak.
  For thee, against myself I speak,
  To show thy faults what they are.


