Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
So, you, in your bloody errors, forget
The very thing that binds you to me,
And wretched errors grow Salvaged like ragged garments,
On second thought, the errors are knit anew,
And strength by limping sway does wrack.
But why should I care if your deepest longings
Or nerves from beneath your breast do lie?
Or on your lively outer side do I care,
When all I long for is your inward glow?
  Love is a babe. Then, nothing I can do,
  But what I do, like a willing nurse.


