In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Mine own real love that mak'steth mine eye false.
For mine own goodness do define the greater part of me,
Thy image holds the greater part of me;
For all mine is thine, and thine alone,
Methinks no harm can do me nor thee.
In this connection, my liberty is so great,
That I may not on thy part do rulers' eyes,
Since thou art all my subjects to me.
  But what's so blessed-fair that so guards
  Thou none but mine own doing?


