Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To catch the escaped child before it is taken away.
So you, in your cunning thoughts, should not unsettle
My heart, with abandon, that it may wander free,
From this ballet of fear, into you.
No more shall I fear, run after you,
When you have swiftly moved past me,
While clutching my heart, with vigilance cautioned,
As a devoted nurse would her cherished host.
  Fear not to claim my heart, for it is thine,
  Given freely, and never to rescind.


