Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To the nest of her frenzied heart and brain.
But if the chick survives, resumes her part,
She belongs to the flock, and you, her hope,
Are left, my joy, your sorrow, to me.
Oh, should you pass, childless, from this earth's relief,
The world shall wail and gnash its teeth in despair,
Lamenting the void left by your form unseen,
While every private widow, in her quiet lair,
Can treasure her beloved, kept evergreen.
