Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may have him as a debtor;
But that he maintains such tenancy is not my concern,
But his due award me under possession of thee.
So, thou art so enforced by his willful will,
