Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To the place where she thinks her least wanted child will be.
So you, in your unstrung privilege,
Cannot make me run after you;
Come what may, your baby shall find out,
If fate or my love shall meet.
Unlooked for joy in that I may not know you,
So guarded against unknown hands doing thee wrong,
Do not even so much as whisper to me your name,
When I am sometime absent from thy heart,
  Lest I, too much profane, should do it wrong
  And haply of our old acquaintance tell.


