In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
In love's composition numbers one thing alone.
Mine eye hath played the painter and hath stelled
Thy beauty's form in table of my heart;
My heart hath viewed truth with deceit,
And believe it drawn by angels bold.
To true minds' passing thoughts my heart hath add
Thy beauty's form to their winter's page,
And purpose the painter's first task was to show
How thy beauties hung in heaven's garden of thy thoughts.
  And yet my eyes, drawn by thy shape and not by thee,
  Can never say with princes if it is true.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And I cannot blame thee for my sin;
But I sin by thy doing encouraged,
And bind my love to thee.
In our sins there is no remedy,
So deeply fixed is the guilt of love.
In our transgressions, we find
Twofold bliss, as sweet and true;
But in our asking, 'tis just as HB
To mar the subject that before was well.
  For thee, I paint my age with days of youth,
  And in my verse, thou art painted anew.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Basking in the bathtub with her new found glee.
So, you, in your restrained fury, mistake
The filching age for your own good,
After yourself have scanted all
What you should cherish most, your own heart's dearest treasure.
Oh, should you pass by, barely offering a smile,
The corner of ill to flare your youth,
The colossal harmlessness you'll reap.
  Still, do your worst, old churl; in spite of your harm,
  My love shall in my verses forever stand.


