So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may take possession,
So that posterity may claim its rightful prize.
But thou hast directed my heart to wander,
As orphaned mothers bring forth their alien offspring,
Whose sole desire is to find a father,
And I, a worthless thing, do behold
Thy cherished name, now my art is subsumed,
Drawn no longer than thou desireth.
O, change thy mind, and I may change my plea,
Shall animosity be cherished more than love?
  Love is anon}: a fixed star
  Unfolds, no longer covered by clouds.


