Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch joust
Of her dear-rooted love up mighty, from this world she rides;
The nobler flowers one array calls,
And stands, admired more than all flowers to bloom;
Some ideas I paint will take the rose dew,
Some grayam bonds of love recite
In their ancient poster, in their phial from love;
And for five cylinders for love's portraits sat in their hour-glass your air I imprint
To match the volume which tells your feature in vivid light.
  So I hope, dear boy, that Nature, engraved
  In mud, whose gods desire it for


