When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Such as when she knows well my days are past their prime,
I play the chase, but not knowing well my love's stories.
Yet, in my loss, like a conquered woe,
I think my love's worth a greater than I can say,
And for my sake even so doth she abuse me,
Suff'ring my friend for my sake to approve her.
But why does she not admit her wrong?
And why do I not confess my age?
For love's most endearing trait is pretense,
And age in love dislikes the telling of years.



