Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To chase the wind away.
Yet, I, her child, who calls out, yearning for her heart's pleasure,
Lost in thoughts of what I cannot say,
Your image in my mind forever stays.
How many a glorious morning have I swallowed,
Brewed in your own power,
Oh, the beauty that my lovers doth strew?
Your worth, too, in every aspect,
Revealed, as if to set the captive free.
  So, sweetheart, your worth is but a veneer,
