In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the disapproval of my eyes, it offers no surrenders.
My ears find no allure in your voice's symphony,
Nor do gentle emotions yearn for the lowly touch;
Nor taste or scent, seek to indulge in the sensual spree,
In any lustful feast with you in the spot and clutch.
My five senses and my wisdom cannot,
Dissuade one infatuated heart from serving thee,
Unmoved, the semblance of a man, fate has been cast,
Thy heart's loyal subject, a wretch, ever bound to thee.



Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Thy virtue hath my duty strongly knit.
That I do not blame in using what I think good,
Lest I be blamed, let not those lips part,
Adorned with hues of deceit, utter reproof.
For to thee it is a home of love
A keepsake for thee, of our recompense,
Suspecting that the true love will be lost,
As interest for a painted counterfeit.
  For fear of which, hear this written word,
  A thousand groans, but thinking on thy name.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To work the lines that every alien land.
Yet, I, her husband, watch her blood warm,
Her eyes, their source, in her quiet lair,
By children's eyes, her husband's shape in mind.
I tell the mirror, you'll find the source
Of Love's renewal, the eternal rain,
If not rejuvenated, then flows no more,
Our love shall never die.
  In love's own power, you'll gain a pearl,
  A keepsake for you, of our recompense.


