Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch;
Her beloved walks gracefully alone,
One emotion it cannot repress,
Another cry she lacks to chase.
Her heart is full, then empty, sad,
In love's game, to match hearts, once all lay.
No tidings of this well-versed dance
Can bring me to rest or outlive
My familiar writings.
  Yet, should you read this humble verse,
  I shall survive, born of love's sweet seeds.


