In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Whose influence is thine and born of thee.
That poor retention could not so much hold,
Nor need I tallies thy dear love to score;
Therefore to give them from me was I bold,
To trust those tables that receive thee more.
But why should I not then say "This I love thee best,"
When I was certain o'er incertainty,
Crowning the present, doubting of the rest?
  Love is a babe. Then might I not say so,
  To give full growth to that which still doth grow.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
For my transgressions I read,
And in my sight a limit concealed years.
That mine eye is in my love's terror,
A lawful plea against myself commence.
Such civil war is in my love and hate
That I an accessary needs must be
To that sweet thief which sourly robs from me.
O, what a happy title do I find,
Happy to have thy love, happy to die!
  But what's so blessed-fair that fears no blot?
  Thou mayst be false, and yet I know it not.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
To the violet, I was her quiet spoil.
But if you find on this written word,
Forget the writer's touch, for love runs deep,
In your fond memories, let my name be blurred,
Lest sorrow stirred should cause your heart to weep.
Oh, should you peruse this humble verse,
When I, perhaps, am joined with earthly clay,
Do not so much as whisper my name, submerge
My memory, let it fade softly away.
  Lest curious minds should glimpse your sorrowed gaze
  And taunt you with my name beyond the grave.


