Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine eye
May hold my dear love with tender care.
But since he belongs to thee,
Mine own will be thy widow and still weep
That thou no form of thee hast left behind,
When every private widow well may keep,
By children's eyes, her husband's shape in mind.
But since he pricked thee out for women's prize,
The sole effect is thine and born of thee.
  Look what is best, that best I wish in thee.
  This wish I have, then ten times happy me.


