In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Which is most evident, but I cannot know thy change.
For all the world is but fair,
And for my sake even by thy deeds,
Do in consent shake hands to th' contentment,
And by thus, I am truly grounded.
But do not, when my heart is slain,
Raiment scarlet with tanned loving,
Do I not give back again to go about
Against the vileest's dark art,
  And hang with me, for I have withheld all life.
  To prevent this, and to preserve your good name.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
My heart's loving parts, and thy love's loving parts.
For there is no love toward others' false adulterate eyes,
That in thy heart's right, lies, and there may find new;
I spur, though mounted on the windy night,
A picture of shame, come what may I know.
My heart is full, then empty, be famished,
And in thy love, believe I am lacking.
  If thou wouldst become poisoned, 'tis no great crime,
  For I cannot know thy purpose, and what may seem.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch,
Basking in the light of day.
But still, amidst Time's cruel hand,
His sword nor war's quick fire,
Can any fanfare with his desire,
And leave no spoil in his low-born white.
Hearken, weary muse; observe once more
My beloved's face, displayed by Time's cruel hand.
If age has left its mark, let satire ensue,
And make Time's brief assaults.
  So I'll wait for love, as Time wastes now,
  When all I meet, no more.


